  "title": "Starbucks Unionization Debate",
  "objective": "Simulate tensions between corporate, employees, and customers during Starbucks' unionization wave",
  "brief": "Starbucks unionization wave (2021-2023). Over 300 stores voted to unionize, starting from a single Buffalo store, while corporate mounted aggressive counter-campaigns including store closures and firing organizers. Stakeholders: a barista-organizer working two jobs to cover rent who was written up for 'tardiness' after organizing meetings, a store manager caught between corporate directives to discourage unions and personal loyalty to their staff, a longtime customer and disability advocate concerned about service changes if experienced baristas leave, and a commercial real estate analyst tracking store closure patterns that correlate with union votes.",
